Git is a version control system used to track code changes.
It helps developers manage and maintain source code.
Git is distributed, so every developer has a local copy of the repository.
A repository (repo) stores the project files and their history.
git init creates a new Git repository.
git add stages changes for commit.
git commit saves changes with a message.
git push uploads local changes to a remote repository.
git pull downloads and updates changes from a remote repository.
Git helps teams work together, track changes, and restore previous versions
